Defect from Green 1.6:
The D-7 case "clears the example text on edit but keeps the figures" used
test.tsx:193  expect(screen.queryByText("15,000")).not.toBeNull();
and failed with "Found multiple elements with the text: 15,000". For five own
students, no legs, and the 3,000 price, spec 5.3 item 6 and D-3 render 15,000
twice: the results.ownGV row and the results.networkGV row. A single-element
query cannot pass against a spec-conformant component.

Correction applied (test file only):
const results = resultRegion();
expect(within(results).getAllByText("15,000")).toHaveLength(2);
The check is scoped to the polite live-region result card and requires exactly
two matches. This keeps the meaning: the example figure stays after an edit,
and both spec rows are now proven to render it. Every other assertion, case
name, and the copy import are unchanged.

